Spec: Android gateway platform

Purpose:
  Develop Android application integration separately from the installed legacy gateway.

Owns:
  ./settings.gradle
  ./build.gradle

Structure:
  ./app: Existing paired transport application.
  ./broker-dev: Isolated development-only Binder negotiation application.
  ./control-ipc: Shared generated AIDL contract.
  ./public-contracts: Portable Java contracts build bridge.
  ./registration-core: Portable pending transaction core and desktop SQLite verification.
  ./client: Signature-pinned Android pending registration client SDK.
  ./secure-transport: Portable Java device transport and interoperability build bridge.
  ./agent-core: Mobile authority and real SQLite conformance build bridge.
  ./agent: Keystore-backed authenticated access Agent with private foreground ownership.
  ./client-streams: Thin private descriptor and Java socket SDK without Agent secrets.
  ./descriptor-core: Shared descriptor ownership and bounded framing without authority dependencies.
  ./native-consumer: Independently signed SDK-only native integration fixture.
  ./control-authority: Agent-only standard server lease verification build bridge.

References:
  /docs/SPEC.md
  /docs/SECURITY-SPEC.md

Must:
  Keep legacy package identity, version and transport components unchanged during Binder development.
  Use AGP9.1.1 and Gradle9.3.1 with JDK17 for the authenticated Agent's API37 HTTP dependency; compile platform updates must not silently raise minSdk or targetSdk.
